<code>assert \forall int i; i>=0; this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) ^ set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the comment: for every valid bit index, the value after XOR equals the XOR of its original value and the corresponding bit in the argument set. XOR of two booleans can be expressed with `!=`.

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) != set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
Looking at the XOR operation, the assertion needs to express that for every valid bit index, the resulting bit equals the XOR of its original value and the corresponding bit in the argument set.

XOR of two booleans `a` and `b` can be written as `a != b`.

<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) != set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; 0<=i && i<this.size(); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) ^ set.get(i));</code>
--------------------
